{{!
    @template local_accessibility/tile

    One tile: its icon, name and current value in words (choices spec §2). A drawer tile controls its drawer
    (local_accessibility/drawer, rendered by the panel); a detail tile opens its view. Behaviour is in
    local_accessibility/panel.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * id - tile id (a feature id, or "spacing" for the three spacing features)
    * label, icon - the tile's name and Font Awesome icon
    * kind - "drawer" or "detail"; isdrawer - whether kind is "drawer"
    * valuetext - the current value in words
    * active - whether any member differs from its default
    * locked - whether the admin locked the tile
    * iscolour - the colour tile, which shows the low-contrast warning icon
    * lowcontrast - resolved from the panel context: exact custom colours under 7:1 show the warning icon

    Example context (json):
    {"id": "spacing", "label": "Spacing", "icon": "fa-arrows-up-down", "kind": "detail", "isdrawer": false,
     "valuetext": "Line 1.8 · Letter 0.12", "active": true, "locked": false, "iscolour": false,
     "members": ["lineheight", "letterspacing", "wordspacing"]}
}}
<button type="button" class="la-tile" data-tile="{{id}}" data-kind="{{kind}}"
        aria-label="{{label}}, {{valuetext}}"
        {{#isdrawer}}aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="la-drawer-{{id}}"{{/isdrawer}}
        {{#active}}data-active="true"{{/active}} {{#locked}}aria-disabled="true"{{/locked}}>
    <i class="icon fa {{icon}}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <span class="la-label" aria-hidden="true">{{label}}</span>
    <span class="la-value" aria-hidden="true">{{valuetext}}</span>
    {{#locked}}<i class="icon fa fa-lock la-lock" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{/locked}}
    {{#iscolour}}<i class="icon fa fa-triangle-exclamation la-warn" aria-hidden="true" {{^lowcontrast}}hidden{{/lowcontrast}}></i>{{/iscolour}}
</button>
